/**
 * The emblem, embedded, for the invoice and credit note PDFs.
 *
 * A BASE64 CONSTANT RATHER THAN A FILE READ, and that is the whole reason this
 * file exists. @react-pdf/renderer will happily take a path, but these documents
 * are rendered inside serverless functions where `public/` is served as static
 * assets and is not part of the function bundle — so a path that works locally
 * would produce an invoice with no logo in production, and only for real
 * customers. A data URI cannot fail differently in the two places.
 *
 * 180×162 from public/logo_emblem_transparent.png, which is 3096px wide.
 * It prints 39.6pt tall, which puts this at very nearly 300dpi at print size —
 * chosen by rendering the mark at 34, 44 and 56pt and looking at all three: below
 * about 44pt the interlaced strands close up and the weave stops reading as a
 * weave. The full-size original would have added 400kB to every render for it.
 *
 * To regenerate after a brand change:
 *
 *   sips -Z 180 public/logo_emblem_transparent.png --out /tmp/emblem.png
 *   node -e 'const fs=require("fs");console.log(fs.readFileSync("/tmp/emblem.png").toString("base64"))'
 *
 * and paste the result below, keeping the width and height in step.
 */

